#. i18n: file: kmymoney/wizards/newaccountwizard/kaccounttypepagedecl.ui:23
#. i18n: ectx: property (text), widget (K3ActiveLabel, kActiveLabel4)
#: rc.cpp:4358
msgid ""
"Enter the name of the account under which it is known within KMyMoney. "
"Select the type for the new account. Use the <b>What's this?</b> feature to "
"see more details about the various account types. Enter the date the account "
"was opened and its currency."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file: kmymoney/wizards/newaccountwizard/kaccounttypepagedecl.ui:40
#. i18n: ectx: property (whatsThis), widget (KMyMoneySecuritySelector, m_currencyComboBox)
#: rc.cpp:4361
msgid "Select the currency in which this account is denominated."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file: kmymoney/wizards/newaccountwizard/kaccounttypepagedecl.ui:79
#. i18n: ectx: property (whatsThis), widget (kMyMoneyEdit, m_openingBalance)
#: rc.cpp:4370
msgid ""
"The opening balance is the balance of the account when you start using it "
"with KMyMoney. For new accounts this is usually 0 but for existing accounts "
"this may well differ. Please consult the account statements to figure out "
"this value. The opening balance is to be provided in the currency of the "
"account as selected with the currency button."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file: kmymoney/wizards/newaccountwizard/kaccounttypepagedecl.ui:101
#. i18n: ectx: property (whatsThis), widget (kMyMoneyDateInput, m_openingDate)
#: rc.cpp:4376
msgid ""
"The opening date would be the date of the last statement. In case you want "
"to keep track of transactions prior to this date, enter the ending balance "
"and statement date of a prior statement and add all following transactions "
"into KMyMoney.\n"
"<br>\n"
"<i>Note</i>: If you do not know the exact amount of the opening balance, "
"enter an estimate. You can change this value later before you reconcile this "
"account for the first time."
msgstr ""

#. i18n: file: kmymoney/wizards/newaccountwizard/kaccounttypepagedecl.ui:118
#. i18n: ectx: property (text), widget (QLabel, textLabel2_2)
#: rc.cpp:4384
